# Trivy findings that are deliberate decisions, each with its reason.
#
# Anything listed here is a conscious trade-off, not an oversight. If a reason
# stops being true, delete the line and fix the finding.

# CloudFront access logging.
# Off by default because it writes billable S3 objects continuously for a site
# whose whole design target is effectively zero cost. It is a variable:
# set enable_cloudfront_access_logs = true to turn it on.
AVD-AWS-0010

# CloudFront WAF.
# A WAF is a standing monthly charge well beyond this project's cost target,
# and the distribution serves only static, public, read-only content with no
# forms, no authentication and no request-time backend. A CloudFront pricing
# plan may attach its own managed ACL, which the distribution tolerates.
AVD-AWS-0011

# S3 bucket logging.
# Access logging on the site and data buckets would write billable objects for
# traffic that CloudFront already fronts. Both buckets are private, readable
# only by this distribution through Origin Access Control.
AVD-AWS-0089

# Customer-managed KMS key for S3.
# There are no secrets in this system: it publishes public Parliamentary
# information. SSE-S3 encrypts at rest without the standing monthly charge of
# a customer-managed key.
AVD-AWS-0132
